on at intended area (eczema, psoriasis, rash)\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Hepatitis B / C, HIV or other bloodborne condition\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Immunocompromised / undergoing chemotherapy / radiotherapy\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Currently taking antibiotics, steroids, or immunosuppressants\u0027,\r\n    \u0027History of fainting / vasovagal episodes\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Haemophilia or clotting / bleeding disorder\u0027\r\n  ],\r\n  tattoo:[\r\n    \u0027Previous allergic reaction to tattoo ink (specify colour if known)\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Skin condition affecting healing (vitiligo, psoriasis, lichen planus)\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Had radiation therapy in or near intended tattoo area\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Currently taking or recently stopped isotretinoin / Roaccutane (must pause 6 months)\u0027,\r\n    \u0027MRI scan planned — inform your radiologist of new tattoo\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Organ transplant recipient or on anti-rejection medication\u0027\r\n  ],\r\n  piercing:[\r\n    \u0027Previous keloid or raised scar from a piercing\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Severe nickel or metal allergy\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Current infection, swelling, or open wound at intended piercing site\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Oral hygiene concerns — relevant for tongue / lip piercings\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Heart valve condition / endocarditis risk — antibiotic prophylaxis may be required\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Hemophilia or prolonged bleeding tendency\u0027\r\n  ],\r\n  pmu:[\r\n    \u0027Previous allergic reaction to PMU pigment, tattoo ink, or patch test failure\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Fitzpatrick skin type V or VI — discuss pigment selection with artist\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Active acne, rosacea, or perioral dermatitis in treatment area\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Currently using retinol, tretinoin, or AHA/BHA near treatment area\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Botox or dermal fillers within last 4 weeks in or near treatment area\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Laser skin treatment planned in treatment area within 4 weeks\u0027,\r\n    \u0027Trichotillomania (hair